v 3
d 'CROSSWALK_MULTICLASS': module providing crosswalk tables to translate ISCO-88com and ISCO-08 into the MultiClass class schemes
d
d crosswalk_multiclass is an add-on for the crosswalk package by Ben
d Jann. It provides crosswalk tables translating ISCO-88com and ISCO-08
d occupational codes into class schemes of the MultiClass schema:
d MicroSEC (30 classes), the meso-class scheme (18 classes), the ESeC
d multi-purpose variant ESeC-MP (11 classes), and, for ISCO-08, a
d 77-category micro-class scheme. MicroSEC, meso-class and ESeC-MP are
d defined jointly over occupation and employment relation, so those
d tables carry one destination column per employment status, and two
d case functions are supplied to construct that argument; the
d micro-class scheme is purely occupational and takes no case. Tables
d are provided for 4-digit ISCO codes and, directly, for 3-digit ISCO
d minor groups. The schemes nest: MicroSEC, the meso-class and ESeC-MP
d each aggregate to the European Socio-economic Classification (ESeC).
d This package does not duplicate plain ESeC itself, since crosswalk
d already provides isco88_to_esec() and isco08_to_esec(); see help
d crosswalk_multiclass for details and the correct case functions to use
d with them. The package contains no ado-file and defines no command of
d its own; all recoding is carried out by the crosswalk command.
d
d KW: ISCO-88com
d KW: ISCO-08
d KW: occupation
d KW: social class
d KW: ESeC
d KW: ESeC-MP
d KW: MicroSEC
d KW: micro-class
d KW: meso-class
d KW: class scheme
d KW: crosswalk
d
d Requires: Stata version 14 and crosswalk, moremata from SSC (q.v.)
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260818
d
d Author: Oscar Smallenbroek
d
f crosswalk_multiclass.sthlp
